{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MirrorPairBondScaling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MirrorPairBondScaling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.li7_be7_pairwise_prediction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.li7_be7_pairwise_prediction","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L94-L100","doc":"**New prediction, ⁷Li/⁷Be**: `(Z,d,A) = (3,1,7)`, so `m = 6`, giving the\npairwise mirror ratio `(a/b)⁶`. (Pairwise `b₂` level only — the large exponent is\nthe model's explicit over-scaling for heavier mirrors, not a closure.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.triton_helium3_recovered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.triton_helium3_recovered","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**Recovery of the A=3 identity** `triton_helium3_split`: `(Z,d,A) = (1,1,3)`,\nso `m = A−1 = 2`, giving the T/³He split `(a/b)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mirror_pair_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mirror_pair_split","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L77-L85","doc":"**Mirror-pair isospin split (general law).** For the mirror pair\n`(Z, Z+d) ↔ (Z+d, Z)` (isospin gap `d`, shared mass number, shared multiplicity\n`m = A−1`), the aggregate ratio is exactly `(a/b)^{d·m}` — the split a type-blind\nbond model gives as `1`. Requires `a, b ≠ 0` (the traces are nonzero at `q₀`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondTraceProduct_eq_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondTraceProduct_eq_pow","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L69-L75","doc":"**Scaling law.** The bond-trace product is a single `m`-th power of the\nnucleon-content monomial: `bondTraceProduct Z N m = (a^Z · b^N)^m`. The entire\npairwise cluster level is governed by the one exponent `m = A−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pairAggregate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pairAggregate","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The pairwise **aggregate** of `(Z,N)`: the product of the inverse-product bond\nweights, i.e. the reciprocal of the bond-trace product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondTraceProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondTraceProduct","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The **bond-trace product** of a nucleus `(Z,N)`: the product of `τx·τy` over\nall pairwise bonds, whose collapsed exponents are `Z·m` on `a` and `N·m` on `b`\nwith `m := A−1`. Kept with the multiplicity `m` free (a `ℕ`), so no\n`ℕ`-subtraction enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondWeightM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondWeightM","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorPairBondScaling.lean#L55-L56","doc":"Inverse-product (Mayer ideal-gas) bond weight `w(x,y) = 1/(x·y)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}